      "description": "Root cause. The row-mt error signal derives the row index directly from `xd->mi_row` and the current tile start without validating that `xd->mi_row` still belongs to that tile. When an earlier internal error leaves `xd->mi_row` stale, this expression becomes negative and drives the out-of-bounds row-sync write."
